        "market_text": "<p>California is not one market — a Noe Valley Victorian, a Sacramento new build and an Orange County family home attract different buyers with different taste. What they share is price point: with the median California home among the most expensive in the nation, buyers expect listing photos that look like the money being asked.</p><p>Physical staging costs scale with those prices — often thousands per month in coastal metros. Virtual home staging delivers the same first impression once, for {price:virtual-staging} a photo, which is why California agents were among our first and remain our largest client base.</p><p>The state also has the clearest disclosure expectations in the country, which is a good thing for agents who want to use staged photos without second-guessing. AB 723 set the standard, and our California work is built to it — disclosure guidance ships with the order rather than being something you assemble afterward.</p>",
